{"timestamp":"2026-09-28T18:44:14.277Z","ordinal":1499,"type":"response_item","payload":{"type":"custom_tool_call","id":"ctc_06bf2485f54c8e3f016abab57e379c87d19fd615e96570955f","status":"completed","call_id":"call_c10UhsoFuvC8qs1ThyEhkmqt","name":"exec","input":"text(await tools.apply_patch(\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /home/ubuntu/cd3-code-audit/README.md\\n+# CD3 Hybrid Source and Binary Audit\\n+\\n+## Result\\n+\\n+The two existing rate-1.4 cores expose a concrete under-sized capacity check\\n+inside the loaded CUDA driver's batched-copy command emitter. This is more\\n+specific evidence than merely observing a crash in `libcuda` or a successful\\n+serialized run. No serving run or synthetic CUDA experiment was performed\\n+for this audit. Production code and experiment settings were not changed.\\n+\\n+The application submits variable-length segment spans. The driver checks space\\n+using a cached command-size estimate plus 1,152 bytes, but its inline-copy\\n+emitter writes the current payload plus its command header. In both cores,\\n+the checked size fits and the actual emitted size does not.\\n+\\n+| Existing core | Cached estimate | Checked bytes (+1152) | Writable bytes remaining | Actual bytes needed |\\n+| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\\n+| Original pipeline, 20260928T144024Z | 3660 | 4812 | 12108 | 21420 |\\n+| Second pipeline, 20260928T181012Z | 6276 | 7428 | 14012 | 16164 |\\n+\\n+Actual bytes needed here are 32 bytes of fixed header, one 4-byte inline\\n+packet header, and the current payload: 21,384 or 16,128 bytes respectively.\\n+Both payloads fit in a single emitter chunk (maximum 32,764 bytes).\\n+\\n+The immediate failure mechanism is therefore an internal command-buffer\\n+overrun, not an application request to copy past the end of a 64-KiB segment.\\n+This audit identifies the failing size calculation in the installed binary;\\n+it is not a vendor-confirmed bug report or proof of a particular fixed version.\\n+\\n+## Application Path\\n+\\n+Source files in this directory are inspection copies of the current container\\n+checkout, not a second deployed implementation. Baseline commit:\\n+`aaa16a378cb1194bb5cdc161e05c81e359dbf48e`, plus the existing Nsight patch and\\n+the already-added opt-in serial diagnostic.\\n+\\n+1. `tiered_serve/compression/cuda/chunk_delta3_hybrid.h:1021` selects and sorts\\n+   exception entries by segment and byte offset. Lines 1051-1071 merge only\\n+   adjacent entries in the same segment, producing variable-length copies.\\n+2. `chunk_delta3_hybrid.h:540` submits the K and V batches on the H2D stream,\\n+   then queues their decoders with K/V completion-event dependencies.\\n+3. `tiered_serve/compression/cuda/chunk_delta3_ext.cpp:1023` passes these sizes\\n+   to `cudaMemcpyBatchAsync`, with one valid stream-order attribute covering\\n+   the batch. CUDA 13's eight-argument signature is used.\\n+4. `tiered_serve/compression/cuda/chunk_delta3_csr_serial.h:232` instead adds\\n+   each side's contiguous CSR exception arena as one copy. CSR and hybrid\\n+   share the GPU decode kernel but differ in exception-copy shape and stream\\n+   scheduling. CSR success does not exercise the same descriptor sequence.\\n+\\n+The native code does not branch on request rate. A different arrival rate can\\n+change active rows, selected segment spans, copy lengths, and command-buffer\\n+position. The demonstrated failure requires the checked size to fit while\\n+the current emitted command does not. Thus rate 1.6 succeeding does not\\n+contradict this mechanism. Its precise successful command sequence was not\\n+reconstructed, so this is a mechanistic explanation, not an observed trace\\n+of the avoided boundary in that successful run.\\n+\\n+## Driver Instructions\\n+\\n+Binary: `/usr/local/cuda-13.2/compat/libcuda.so.1`, package 595.45.04.\\n+SHA-256: `e83bb4f47a079d86ba6c2e04449430b0bc1c852904e2cf53ae1995b2e76c91e0`.\\n+Addresses below are the second core's virtual addresses. Function/variable\\n+names in the pseudocode are explanatory, not recovered NVIDIA source names.\\n+\\n+The batch loop initializes `[sp+328]` at `0xf525535f638c`; subsequent\\n+iterations branch to `0xf525535f63a0`, after that initialization.\\n+\\n+```text\\n+0xf525535f6fc4  ldr  w1, [sp, #328]       ; cached size estimate\\n+0xf525535f6fcc  cbnz w1, ...7a44\\n+0xf525535f7a44  add  w2, w1, #0x480       ; estimate + 1152\\n+0xf525535f7a58  bl   0xf525535092b0       ; capacity checker\\n+0xf525535f7a68  b.eq ...7b80               ; insufficient-space branch\\n+```\\n+\\n+The capacity checker uses that argument to update the reserved end position.\\n+It does not receive the current payload length. The emitter, in contrast,\\n+receives the current length from the sizes array, constructs an inline packet,\\n+and copies that many bytes into the command buffer.\\n+\\n+```text\\n+0xf52553511b60  add  x6, x0, #0x20        ; fixed header = 32 bytes\\n+0xf52553511b88  cmp  w21, w25              ; chunk limit = 32764 bytes\\n+0xf52553511bb4  str  w3, [x6], #4         ; inline header = 4 bytes\\n+0xf52553511bbc  str  wzr, [x6, x0, lsl #2]; zero last payload word: FAULT\\n+0xf52553511bc0  mov  x0, x6\\n+0xf52553511bc4  bl   ...                   ; payload memcpy\\n+```\\n+\\n+After emission, the caller retains a nonzero cached estimate instead of\\n+increasing it to the size just emitted:\\n+\\n+```text\\n+0xf525535f7024  sub  x25, x0, x25         ; bytes actually emitted\\n+0xf525535f7028  ldr  w2, [sp, #328]\\n+0xf525535f7030  cmp  w2, #0\\n+0xf525535f7034  csel w0, w2, w25, ne      ; retain old nonzero estimate\\n+0xf525535f7038  str  w0, [sp, #328]\\n+```\\n+\\n+For this path, the behavior is equivalent to:\\n+\\n+```c\\n+if (cached_estimate != 0) {\\n+    if (!has_capacity(cursor, cached_estimate + 1152))\\n+        goto obtain_more_space;\\n+}\\n+next = emit_copy(cursor, current_source, current_destination, current_size);\\n+if (cached_estimate == 0)\\n+    cached_estimate = next - cursor;\\n+cursor = next;\\n+```\\n+\\n+This is a partial reconstruction of the observed branch, not the complete\\n+driver algorithm. Other transfer types and allocation branches exist.\\n+\\n+## Second Core Arithmetic\\n+\\n+The capacity-checker's own retained state independently matches the undersized\\n+check, rather than only the crash register values:\\n+\\n+- Command allocation: 4,194,304 bytes, ending at `0x200c00000`.\\n+- Current subrange begins at allocation offset 4,089,108 (`0x3e6514`).\\n+- Remaining subrange capacity: 105,196 bytes.\\n+- Current command cursor: `0x200bfc944`, offset 91,184 within the subrange.\\n+- Cached estimate: 6,276 bytes; checked size: 7,428 bytes.\\n+- Recorded reserved end: 98,612 (`0x18134`) = 91,184 + 7,428.\\n+- Required end: 107,348 = 91,184 + 16,164, exceeding capacity by 2,152 bytes.\\n+- Payload begins at `0x200bfc968`; last 4-byte store faults at `0x200c00864`.\\n+\\n+The original core has the same instruction and the same under-check pattern:\\n+command cursor `0x200bfd0b4`, payload start `0x200bfd0d8`, last store\\n+`0x200c0245c`. The original source descriptor was independently checked against\\n+its live segment: 21,384 bytes within a 65,536-byte segment, matching generation,\\n+29 record references, and one reader lease.\\n+\\n+Full batch-loop disassembly and capacity-checker output are saved alongside\\n+this report. Core analysis reads the existing crashed processes; it does not\\n+launch the serving workload.\\n+\\n+## Other Source Checks\\n+\\n+- Segment append reserves a disjoint range and increments a record reference\\n+  before copying; publication occurs after that copy. Reader leases prevent\\n+  segment recycling while a plan's H2D remains in flight.\\n+- Fixed body writes wait for the layer's previous H2D completion in\\n+  `chunk_delta3_kv_compressor.py:1956`. GPU staging reuse waits for the ring's\\n+  decode-consumed event in `chunk_delta3_hybrid.h:538`.\\n+- CPU exception writes are capacity-bounded; overflow records are handled by\\n+  the existing raw fallback. The kernel is shared with CSR. No concrete normal-\\n+  path overrun in those routines was found in this inspection.\\n+- The process-wide `stack_pool.c:32` and `:48` hooks remain independently unsafe:\\n+  the free list lacks synchronization, `munmap` accepts untracked addresses\\n+  solely by size, and reuse ignores requested protection/flags. These are real\\n+  defects but are not needed to explain the demonstrated under-sized check.\\n+- The sibling PyTorch source is clean at the documented commit\\n+  `70d99e998b4955e0049d13a98d77ae1b14db1f45`. Source cleanliness alone does not\\n+  certify its installed native binary; no new build was performed.\\n+\\n+## Repair Boundary\\n+\\n+An application-side workaround belongs in hybrid H2D submission, not in the\\n+CD3 encoding arithmetic, request rate, capture request index, or segment budget.\\n+Keep segment ownership and the K/V pipeline dependencies intact and avoid the\\n+failing batched-copy emitter path, for example with explicit per-span H2D\\n+submission. That alternative has not been applied or validated by this audit,\\n+and it may change launch overhead. A driver-version replacement likewise needs\\n+independent validation; no fixed version is asserted here. The serial diagnostic\\n+is not a proven fix for this command-size accounting defect.\\n*** End Patch\"));\nfor(const [key,file] of [[\"driver_batch_disassembly\",\"driver-batch-disassembly.txt\"],[\"driver_reserve_analysis\",\"driver-capacity-checker.txt\"]]){\n const value=load(key);text(await tools.apply_patch(\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Add File: /home/ubuntu/cd3-code-audit/\"+file+\"\\n\"+value.split(\"\\n\").map(l=>\"+\"+l).join(\"\\n\")+\"\\n*** End Patch\"));\n}\ntext(await tools.apply_patch(\"*** Begin Patch\\n*** Update File: /home/ubuntu/tieredserve-crash-analysis.md\\n@@\\n # CD3 Hybrid Crash Analysis\\n+\\n+## Source Audit Update\\n+\\n+The later source/binary audit found a concrete under-sized command-buffer\\n+capacity check in the loaded CUDA driver's batched-copy emitter. In both\\n+existing rate-1.4 cores, the cached size used by that check is smaller than the\\n+current inline-copy command; the checked size fits but the actual write crosses\\n+the writable boundary. See `cd3-code-audit/README.md` for the exact instructions,\\n+both cores' arithmetic, and application source links. No new benchmark was run\\n+for that audit. The discussion below records the earlier investigation stage;\\n+its call for more reproductions is not the current diagnostic conclusion.\\n \\n ## Conclusion\\n*** End Patch\"));\n","internal_chat_message_metadata_passthrough":{"turn_id":"01a0e94a-282c-7810-9738-ff9c717d8298","create_time":1790620926.221664}}}
